This study examines the $b 	o u 	au  ar{
u}$ transition, which is a rare process that is highly sensitive to new physics. We investigate the relationship between the new physics couplings in this transition and those in the $b 	o c 	au  ar{
u}$ transition, which is more frequently observed. We find that the new physics couplings in the $b 	o u 	au  ar{
u}$ transition are significantly constrained by the $b 	o c 	au  ar{
u}$ transition.
